        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Local advertising &amp; printed materials</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-3">Business cards, flyers, banners, door hangers, and signage — designed to match your digital ads so your business looks like one brand on a screen and in someone's hand.</p>
        <a href="/en/services/print-materials-treasure-coast/" class="text-xs font-semibold hover:underline" style="color:var(--primary)">Print materials service →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase text-gray-400 mb-10 text-center">Advertising by city</p>
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-20">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 p-6 bg-white">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Vero Beach</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">Advertising in Vero Beach means reaching a market with money to spend and high expectations for how a business looks. Indian River County shoppers compare options carefully before they call, so an advertising company here has to make a small business look as solid as the national brands it competes with — consistent creative across Google and social, and print that matches. We work with Vero Beach boutiques, restaurants, medical and dental practices, and home-service businesses on advertising that fits that standard and still brings in the right customer at a fair cost.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 p-6 bg-white">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Fort Pierce</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">As an advertising agency in Fort Pierce, we build local advertising and digital advertising around St. Lucie County's mix of waterfront businesses, trades, food spots, and community services. Fort Pierce customers tend to trust businesses that feel part of the neighborhood, so we pair tightly targeted Google and Meta campaigns with printed materials for downtown events, the farmers market, and route work. It's also the city where our own organic search visibility is strongest, so paid advertising here builds on ground we already know well.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 p-6 bg-white">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Port St. Lucie</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">Port St. Lucie is the largest and fastest-growing city on the Treasure Coast, with new neighborhoods and new competitors every year. As an advertising agency working here, we keep local advertising — Google Ads, Meta ads, and print — pointed at the specific parts of the city where your customers actually live, instead of paying to reach the whole metro.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 p-6 bg-white">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Stuart</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">We also cover Stuart and the rest of Martin County. If your business is in Stuart, the same services apply — get in touch and we'll put together a plan for your area.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-3 gap-10 mb-20">
      <div class="lg:col-span-2">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase text-gray-400 mb-6">Why a local advertising agency instead of a national one</p>
        <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-5">A national agency treats your account as one row in a system. The campaign comes from a template, your questions go to a ticket queue, and no one on the team has driven US-1 or stood in your parking lot. A local advertising agency knows which street festivals are worth a booth, which ZIP codes to target and which to skip, and how a Vero Beach customer reads an ad differently from a Fort Pierce one.</p>
        <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-5">It also means you can reach a person. A lot of advertising services online are really just a self-serve dashboard — the small business internet advertising customer is left to set the targeting, guess at the budget, and interpret the reports alone. We do that work and then explain it in plain terms: how many people saw the ad, how many contacted you, and what each contact cost.</p>
        <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">We're a small team, so we take on a limited number of clients and stay with them. You get experienced attention on a small-business budget, in English or Spanish, with no long-term contract.</p>
      </div>
